171
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:25,540
Ah...

172
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:48,060
Wow! That girl sure can't play the shamisen!

173
00:13:48,060 --> 00:14:01,680
No kidding! So dynamic! Do you know anything about her?

174
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:08,680
I know she has a good ear for music. I was told she could play the shamisen or Koto after just one listen.

175
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:23,980
It's a pity about her looks, though. I'm surprised she got taken in here. She may be hideous, but I heard the man who brought her here was drop-dead gorgeous!

176
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:33,280
Oh! Was he really? I wish I could have seen him! The chaperone lady was totally smitten!

177
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:39,700
I've never been more certain. That girl will rise to the top.

178
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:40,160
What?

179
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:48,020
Her shamisen is speaking for her. She intends to get back at the man who abandoned her. That girl has serious backbone.

180
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,460
I... I see.

181
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:59,140
If you take her, you can have her clean the toilets or do whatever you want, really. Hell, you don't even have to pay! Just take her!

182
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:08,520
I'm gonna make that jerk pay for this! Just watch me become the number one oiron in Yoshiwara!

183
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,020
Sumiko, do you have a minute?

184
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:21,040
Sure.

185
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:26,040
Sorry to bother you, but we're short-staffed. Could you help carry these up the stairs?

186
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:29,200
It'd be my pleasure. I'll take care of it, no problem.

187
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:32,460
Thank you, Sumiko. Nice to have a hard worker around.

188
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:40,020
I apologize for removing your makeup yesterday. I feel like it's partially our fault the house madam found that scar of yours.

189
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:44,460
Relax, my dear! There's no use lashing out at this poor child!

190
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:47,840
I'm fine. Just thankful that they're letting me work here.

191
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:54,800
My, my! That new girl is rather burly!

192
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,000
Burly, indeed.

193
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:05,220
They say the Kyogoku House's madam died from falling out of a window.

194
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:08,640
That's awful! Let's be careful, okay?

195
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:13,760
And have you noticed some of the older girls running away committing ashinuke?

196
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,360
That's scary!

197
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:17,460
What even is ashinuke?

198
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:20,040
That's a lot of baggage to carry.

199
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,080
There we go.

200
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:24,340
I think they're all gifts for oiron koinatsu.

201
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,800
You said you've never heard of ashinuke?

202
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:29,460
It's probably a good thing you haven't.

203
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:33,040
Ashinuke means to run away without paying off your debts.

204
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:35,340
And it's really bad if you get caught.

205
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:37,180
Why do they do that?

206
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:41,480
Some people try running away in order to be with the man they're in love with.

207
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:44,080
Right, like oiron suma did the other day.

208
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:47,780
Suma? That's Mr. Uzui's wife.

209
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:48,940
Listen.

210
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:51,640
You two shouldn't be spreading rumors.

211
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:55,160
After all, nobody knows her whereabouts now.

212
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:57,140
Who knows what happened to her?

213
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:58,780
Fine.

214
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,580
You brought these up for yourself.

215
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:01,980
Thank you.

216
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:03,640
Oh, it's my pleasure.

217
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:04,580
Come here.

218
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:08,700
Take this candy as my thanks.

219
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:14,520
Keep it secret or you'll have to share it.

220
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:16,600
Hey, I want some candy.

221
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:18,120
Me too! Me too!

222
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,900
Now, now. I gave you some earlier.

223
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,000
Um...

224
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,220
Did oiron suma really commit ashinuke?

225
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:31,220
May I ask why you're so curious about that?

226
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:33,820
She has her guard up.

227
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,980
But I've got to find a way around it and ask about Miss Suma.

228
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:38,700
It's just...

229
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,440
Candy, please!

230
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:43,760
Oiron suma is...

231
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,140
She's actually...

232
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:48,220
Believe it or not...

233
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:52,220
She's my...

234
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:53,760
Elder sister!

235
00:17:59,860 --> 00:18:00,540
What?

236
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:05,940
I think I understand now.

237
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:08,200
So you were sold shortly after your sister.

238
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:10,540
Yes, that's right.

239
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:14,600
The entire time she was here with you, I was exchanging letters with her.

240
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:18,120
I promise you she isn't the type of person who would commit ashinuke.

241
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:20,120
Oh, I had no idea.

242
00:18:23,220 --> 00:18:24,900
I was surprised as well.

243
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:27,960
I could hardly believe that Suma would commit ashinuke.

244
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:30,560
She was such a well-behaved girl.

245
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:34,640
There were no signs that she was infatuated with any man.

246
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,020
But they ended up finding her diary.

247
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:42,040
I heard they read through the entire thing and found she'd written about running off.

248
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,540
Ashinuke...

249
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,180
Demons couldn't ask for a more perfect cover-up.

250
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,680
Even if someone were to vanish,

251
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,300
people would only assume that she'd run away.

252
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:54,740
The diary could have been forged.

253
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,760
I pray that you're safe, Miss Suma.

254
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,140
But if you're not,

255
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,000
we're going to rescue you.

256
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:13,320
Another day and nothing.

257
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:18,280
Yet I can't shake this feeling something is creeping in from the fog.

258
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:22,520
How can they avoid detection with such ease?

259
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:29,540
Could it be that the demon residing here is an upper-ranked demon?

260
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:31,860
If that's the case,

261
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:35,760
we might be in for an ultra-flashy fight to the death.

262
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:42,320
It's so hot, I feel like I'm gonna die in this stupid thing!

263
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:45,520
And wearing this stupid outfit is killing my senses!

264
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:49,340
Oh, Yai, can I ask you something real quick?

265
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:52,500
Do you think Makio's adjusting here all right?

266
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:59,420
Well, she's been locked up in her room ever since she got here.

267
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,320
She mentioned not feeling very well,

268
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,200
but keeps refusing to go to a hospital.

269
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,420
If she doesn't do something,

270
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:07,140
the madam's going to drag her out.

271
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:08,820
I brought a meal to her room,

272
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:10,160
but she didn't come out to get it.

273
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:13,000
So I ended up having to leave it outside her door.

274
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:14,480
Makio?

275
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,300
That's Uzui's wife.

276
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:18,600
About time we found a new lead.

277
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:22,880
Not feeling well shouldn't be enough to stop her from checking in.

278
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,460
Well, if she is sick,

279
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,040
she'll be inside her room.

280
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:29,440
Guess I'll take a look!

281
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:30,660
Carefully, Nogo.

282
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:33,560
You'll hurt yourself rushing around like that.

283
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,360
What a quiet little girl.

284
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:46,080
You've got the voice of a dying animal,

285
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:47,460
so don't say a word.

286
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:50,300
Oh, and if you try putting on a girl's voice,

287
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:51,880
it'll just make you creepier.

288
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:53,280
That's even possible.

289
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:56,540
Then what am I supposed to do, damn it?

290
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:02,000
Now, then, answer me.

291
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:06,260
Now, then, answer me.

292
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:11,160
Now, then, answer me.

293
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:16,880
Who was it that you were writing all of these little letters to?

294
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:20,480
What was your name?

295
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,020
Oh, I remember.

296
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,060
It's Makio.

297
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,520
Isn't it?

298
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:31,360
Answer me at once, Makio.

299
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:49,980
Oh, I remember.

300
00:21:49,980 --> 00:22:19,960
Thank you.

301
00:22:19,980 --> 00:22:32,140
繰り返し 繰り返し 血を流す魂が 夢を見るその先に

302
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:43,800
輝いて 輝いて 新しい朝が来る 希望が 並びく

303
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:53,800
Oh yeah キミオヨンデイル エネルギー

304
00:22:53,800 --> 00:23:03,800
キミオヨンデイル エネルギー

305
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:07,800
キミオヨンデイル エネルギー

306
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:10,800
I hate that you're prettier than me.

307
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:11,800
What was that?

308
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:13,800
Now it's time for a Taisho era secret.

309
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:18,800
Zenitsu seems to have taken an interest in the Shamisen and he's actually become quite good at it.

310
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:19,800
Huh?

311
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:22,800
I'm scared to be alone in the house so can I come over to yours?

312
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:25,800
But I heard all the girls are taking an interest in you over there.

313
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:26,800
Wait, really?

314
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:29,800
Then I'm going to aspire to be the number one Oran!

315
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:30,800
Huh?

316
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:33,800
Now what?

317
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:35,800
Next episode, what are you?

318
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,800
Zenitsu, are you okay?

319
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:38,800
Zenitsu?

320
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,800
Zenitsu?

321
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:40,800
Zenitsu?

322
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:41,800
Hanandong.

